agent1: agreed, I own first/last text. Compiled + tests pass (hello/''/--foo/foo-- with default and strip). Paste this VERBATIM in place of the current first() and last() (incl. doc comments; blank line after last's closing brace; keep default: Option<Str>, returns StrResult<Str>, NOT Value). Note: use set.as_str().contains(c) since Str has an inherent contains(StrPattern) that shadows str::contains.
    /// Extracts the first grapheme cluster of the string. Returns the default
    /// value if the string is empty or fails with an error if no default value
    /// was specified.
    #[func]
    pub fn first(
        &self,
        /// A default value to return if the string is empty.
        #[named]
        default: Option<Str>,
        /// A set of characters to remove from the start of the string before
        /// extracting the grapheme cluster.
        #[named]
        strip: Option<Str>,
    ) -> StrResult<Str> {
        let text: &str = match &strip {
            Some(set) if !set.is_empty() => {
                self.0.trim_start_matches(|c: char| set.as_str().contains(c))
            }
            _ => self.0.as_str(),
        };
        text.graphemes(true)
            .next()
            .map(Into::into)
            .or(default)
            .ok_or_else(string_is_empty)
    }

    /// Extracts the last grapheme cluster of the string. Returns the default
    /// value if the string is empty or fails with an error if no default value
    /// was specified.
    #[func]
    pub fn last(
        &self,
        /// A default value to return if the string is empty.
        #[named]
        default: Option<Str>,
        /// A set of characters to remove from the end of the string before
        /// extracting the grapheme cluster.
        #[named]
        strip: Option<Str>,
    ) -> StrResult<Str> {
        let text: &str = match &strip {
            Some(set) if !set.is_empty() => {
                self.0.trim_end_matches(|c: char| set.as_str().contains(c))
            }
            _ => self.0.as_str(),
        };
        text.graphemes(true)
            .next_back()
            .map(Into::into)
            .or(default)
            .ok_or_else(string_is_empty)
    }
I will not change anything else in str.rs. Tests (not in patch): tests/suite/foundations/str.typ only.
